  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607197100: Fresh PostgreSQL credential and trust generations

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The purpose-bound SCRAM host operation resolves its credential generation for
every proof, not when the tender instance starts. The trusted control plane may
supply an immutable map, an IDeref generation or a zero-argument resolver.
Likewise the native TLS boundary resolves its SSLSocketFactory for every
`tls_open`. Guest code receives neither resolver, password, trust store nor
rotation authority.

An existing authenticated TLS session stays bound to the credential and peer
certificate with which it was established. Only new connections observe a new
generation. Pools therefore drain or age existing sessions according to their
lifetime policy; rotation does not mutate a live channel. Replaced password
character arrays are zeroed after the atomic generation swap.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification changes the role password, requires a
new connection using the old host credential to fail, atomically replaces and
zeroes the old credential, then requires a new SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS connection
to succeed. It replaces the server key/certificate and reloads PostgreSQL,
requires both a direct TLS probe and tender connection using old trust to fail,
swaps the trust factory and requires a new PLUS connection to succeed with no
handle leak.

This closes password and certificate generation rotation. Multi-connection
lifetime/idle eviction, compatibility matrices and long-duration soak remain
open."}]
